{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For it is the ram of ordination.</b> Therefore the right thigh was in this case placed upon the altar — and not so with other offerings — because the right thigh of an animal corresponds to the right hand of a man. It is therefore fitting that the thigh of the offering be upon the altar as a filling of the hand (מלואי יד), corresponding to the right hand of the priest who offers it. For indeed the priest's service was performed with the right hand, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated: wherever 'finger' and 'priesthood' are stated, it means the right hand (Menahot 10a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:31.209559648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}